  "question": "If $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$$ and $3A+2X=B$, find the matrix $X$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "<b>Isolation of the unknown matrix</b><br>From $3A+2X=B$, $$2X=B-3A$$<br><b>Scalar multiplication</b><br>$$3A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Matrix subtraction</b><br>$$B-3A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Required matrix</b><br>$$X=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$$",
  "explanation_image": [],
